    "title": "SCCSD school board to consider naming new interim superintendent - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago SIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — On Thursday, the Sioux City Community School District’s school board is expected to take a step in the search for a new interim superintendent.\nThere are three closed-door sessions scheduled for Thursday. The first one at 5 p.m., then a second session at 5:45 p.m., and the last one at 6:30 p.m.\nStory continues below\nA press release reads that after the third session, the board will decide whether or not to consider a motion for naming an interim top leader of the district.\nThis comes after Dr. Juan Córdova resigned last month after being on paid administrative leave since November, and Angela Bemus went on medical leave .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KCAU 9 News | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
    "summary": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz , 1 hours ago SIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — On Thursday, the Sioux City Community School District’s school board is expected to take a step in the search for a new interim superintendent. The first one at 5 p.m., then a second session at 5:45 p.m., and the last one at 6:30 p.m. A press release reads that after the third session, the board will decide whether or not to consider a motion for naming an interim top leader of the district.",
